  "question": {
    "text": "A stone tide to a string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is whirled in a vertical circle with the other end of the string at the centre. At a certain instant of time, the stone is at its lowest position and has a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math>. The magnitude of change in its velocity, as it reaches a position where the string is horizontal, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0078_796d0e57c556.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 122px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Applying conservation of mechanical energy at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, we get<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Now in vector form.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Therefore, change in velocity will be,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mover><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>u</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mover><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
}